{"feedback":"good","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"😊💖 Aww, that's so sweet of you, Anya! 🍰❤️ Making your mommy's favorite dish, \"arbi ki sabji\" (colocasia stem curry), is a great way to show her how much you care 🤗. I've got a simple and delicious vegan recipe for you to try 📝:<br><br>**Vegan Arbi Ki Sabji Recipe:**<br><br>Ingredients:<br><br>* 250 grams colocasia stems (arbi)\n* 2 medium onions, chopped\n* 2 medium tomatoes, chopped\n* 1 teaspoon cumin seeds\n* 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n* 1 teaspoon garam masala powder\n* 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder\n* 1/2 teaspoon red chili powder (optional)\n* 1/2 teaspoon salt\n* 2 tablespoons vegan oil (e.g., mustard or canola oil)\n* 2 tablespoons vegan yogurt (e.g., soy or coconut-based)\n* Fresh cilantro, chopped (for garnish)<br><br>Instructions:<br><br>1. 🌿 Peel and chop the colocasia stems into bite-sized pieces. Soak them in water for about 30 minutes to reduce their sliminess 🌊.\n2. 🔪 In a pan, heat some oil and sauté the cumin seeds, onions, and tomatoes until they're soft and fragrant 🍅.\n3. 🌮 Add the colocasia stems, coriander powder, garam masala powder, turmeric powder, and salt. Mix well and cook for about 10-12 minutes or until the stems are tender 🥔.\n4. 🌸 Stir in the vegan yogurt and cook for another 2-3 minutes. You can add some water if the curry becomes too thick 🌊.\n5. 🌶️ Taste and adjust the seasoning as needed. Garnish with chopped cilantro and serve hot 💚.<br><br>**Tips and Variations:**<br><br>* You can add some garlic, ginger, or green chilies to the recipe for extra flavor 🧄.\n* If you like a thicker curry, you can add some cornstarch or flour to the vegan yogurt before mixing it in 🌾.\n* Serve with some warm roti, rice, or paratha for a delicious and comforting meal 🍴.<br><br>I hope your mommy loves this vegan arbi ki sabji, and you have a wonderful time celebrating her special day 🎉💖! 💕"}}
